Supported vector index types (service sample environment): DiskANN, HNSW, IVF. The Mongo-style index creation for vectors follows the MongoDB 7.0 kNN index syntax. Example (approximate) command using the mongo shell / pymongo to create an HNSW index on field 'embedding':

db.patient_chunks.createIndex({ embedding: "knnVector" }, {
  name: "embedding_hnsw",
  knnVector: {
    dimension: 1536,
    similarity: "cosine",
    indexType: "hnsw",
    initialCapacity: 10000
  }
})

(Exact option names vary; this is the form expected by MongoDB 7.x-style vector indexes: createIndex with a key value of "knnVector" and knnVector options specifying dimension, indexType (hnsw|ivf|diskann), and metric.)

Basic full-text: use MongoDB text indexes (db.collection.createIndex({field: 'text'}) and queries with $text). For richer/full-featured hybrid vector+text search, use the MongoDB-style $search pipeline stage (Atlas Search-like) with a compound search combining a text operator and a kNN/knnBeta operator, e.g. an aggregation pipeline like:

db.patient_chunks.aggregate([
  { $search: {
      compound: {
        must: [ { text: { query: "pneumonia", path: "text" } } ],
        should: [ { knnBeta: { path: "embedding", vector: [...], k: 10 } } ]
      }
  } },
  { $limit: 10 }
])

If the managed service supports vector search with $search, that pattern provides hybrid ranking; otherwise combine a $text filter with a separate vector similarity aggregation and then re-rank in the application.

Create a kNN vector index on the chunk embedding field. Example mongo shell command (approximate syntax for MongoDB 7-style vector indexes):

db.patient_chunks.createIndex({ embedding: "knnVector" }, {
  name: "embedding_hnsw",
  knnVector: {
    dimension: 1536,
    similarity: "cosine",
    indexType: "hnsw",
    initialCapacity: 10000
  }
})

This index allows efficient nearest-neighbour queries for the vector embeddings stored in 'embedding'.
